{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And the firstborn of the poor shall feed.</b> They are Israel, who were impoverished before every other nation. The meaning is that Israel shall have satiety and dwell securely, and Philistia the opposite." "<b>Your root.</b> The patriarchs." "<b>And your remnant.</b> They are the children. So too לא לאחריתו (Daniel 11:14)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:51.665502403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}